 [:db/cas 17592186308536 :question/problem "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =2,$ and step size $Δx?$  \n\n- The stability function is $R(2Δx)=1-2Δx+2(Δx)^{2}.$\n- The stability region is $|2{(Δx-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n- The method is absolutely stable.\n- The method is stable for step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$" "For the initial value problem ${y}^{′}=f(x,y),y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},$ the modified Euler method can be expressed as the update formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)} & =f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})\\cdot Δx, \\\\ {y}_{n+1} & ={y}_{n}+\\frac{1}{2}(f({x}_{n},{y}_{n})+f({x}_{n+1},{y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}^{(p)}))\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true when testing the stability of the modified Euler method on the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =2,$ and step size $Δx?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The stability function is $R(2Δx)=1-2Δx+2(Δx)^{2}.$\n- **II.** The stability region is $|2{(Δx-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}|<1.$\n- **III.** The method is absolutely stable.\n- **IV.** The method is stable for step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n*Hint:* The stability function $R$ is given by ${y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n}.$"]
